  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrating Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) in Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Netherlands embassy in Jakarta, Indonesia, together with the Netherlands Enterprise (RVO), MVO Nederland, CREM, the Federation of Dutch Exporters (FENEDEX) and the Federation of Dutch Food Industries (FNLI), have developed this proposal for the execution of two parallel projects.1.	The first project aims at exploring the possibilities of standardising CSR in Indonesia. This in a way, that the shift from the charitable sphere to CSR as a business case can be achieved. This, while involving stakeholders from both Dutch and Indonesian backgrounds.More critical consumers have the potential to improve the general business climate in Indonesia. When Indonesian consumers demand more sustainable products, it could incentivise businesses to consider CSR as a business case. This is the first pilot within the larger objective of the first project.2.	The second project focuses on identifying strategies to stimulate sustainable food consumption in Indonesia, as well as exploring opportunities for the Dutch sustainable agri-food sector (including exporters and investors).</narrative>
  </description>
